xfconf_init(): report a failed D-Bus proxy instead of returning TRUE

xfconf_init() created its proxy with a NULL GError and returned TRUE even
when that failed (the daemon could not be activated, say). Every later
property read then ran on a NULL proxy: GLib CRITICALs about NULL errors and
proxies, and no word of the real cause. Pass the error on and fail.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific (bug is generic)

--- a/xfconf/xfconf.c
+++ b/xfconf/xfconf.c
@@ -132,7 +132,13 @@
                                    XFCONF_SERVICE_PATH_PREFIX "/Xfconf",
                                    XFCONF_SERVICE_NAME_PREFIX ".Xfconf",
                                    NULL,
-                                   NULL);
+                                   error);
+    if (!gproxy) {
+        /* Without the proxy every later call fails with a NULL GError
+         * (GLib CRITICALs, no message): report why it could not be made. */
+        g_clear_object(&gdbus);
+        return FALSE;
+    }
 
     ++xfconf_refcnt;
     return TRUE;
